-- Hand-built instance of DerivedFK that deliberately breaks
-- WidgetNameMatches: gadget2's targetname ('gamma') matches no Widget's
-- wname at all, so its derived widget is undefined and
-- g.widget.wname = g.targetname is FALSE for it (undefined never equals
-- a defined value under OCL's total equality) -- WidgetNameMatches
-- reports FAILED. gadget1 still genuinely matches widgetA, so
-- NoMatchIsUndefined ALSO reports FAILED overall (it demands EVERY
-- Gadget's widget be undefined, and gadget1's is not) -- both invariants
-- fail here, unlike PriceCalc's "exactly one" design, because this
-- model's two invariants are near-complementary rather than independent
-- (see valid-instance.soil's own header comment). The validation runner
-- only requires >=1 failure for an "invalid" fixture, so this is still a
-- clean, correctly-classified counterexample.

!create widgetA : Widget
!set widgetA.wname := 'alpha'

!create widgetB : Widget
!set widgetB.wname := 'beta'

!create gadget1 : Gadget
!set gadget1.targetname := 'alpha'

!create gadget2 : Gadget
!set gadget2.targetname := 'gamma'
